# Architecture

## Application shell (do not break)

- Layout: `src/app/layout.tsx` — `SoundInit` + `DesktopLoggingInit` + `AuthProvider` → `AppDataProvider` → `AccessGate` → `AppShell`
- Sidebar: `components/sidebar.tsx` (hidden on auth lock screens and presentation mode)
- Feature pages only fill `{children}` inside the main area

## Data and auth (names only)

- Classroom SSOT: `ClassroomDatabase` via `DatabaseService` (`src/database/database.service.ts`)
- React: `useAppData()` / `AppDataProvider` (`src/store/AppDataContext.tsx`)
- Auth/entitlement: `useAuth()` / `AuthProvider` — not classroom data
- Worker (`workers/cloud-backup`): Google sign-in, entitlements, licensing, optional cloud backup only

Storage details: [persistence.mdc](./persistence.mdc). OAuth/licensing: [docs/ACCOUNTS.md](../../docs/ACCOUNTS.md).

## Routing

- Single shell: Next.js App Router — `src/app/**/page.tsx`
- Tauri desktop loads static export from `out/` (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*` at build time). Targets: Windows x86_64, macOS (aarch64 + x86_64). No Linux desktop releases.

## Next.js 16

- Turbopack is default for `next dev`
- Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` when APIs are ambiguous — not standard Next.js 14/15
- Do not flag `proxy.ts` as a misnamed middleware file on Next.js 16 projects

## Never

- Replace `src/app/layout.tsx` with a standalone feature page
- Remove or hide Sidebar navigation items
- Create a second application layout or entry point
- Move classroom CRUD to the Worker or add enterprise API layers (see [docs/PROJECT_SCOPE.md](../../docs/PROJECT_SCOPE.md))

## Before changing shell, navigation, or persistence

Read: [PROJECT_RULES.md](../../PROJECT_RULES.md), [docs/PROJECT_SCOPE.md](../../docs/PROJECT_SCOPE.md), [docs/DATA_ARCHITECTURE.md](../../docs/DATA_ARCHITECTURE.md), [docs/ACCOUNTS.md](../../docs/ACCOUNTS.md), [docs/build-and-release.md](../../docs/build-and-release.md).
